---
description: Infrastructure and DevOps implementation guidelines, for terraform, ansible among other things.
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
# Infrastructure and DevOps Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_infrastructure
description: Standards for implementing proper infrastructure and DevOps practices
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "(?:Dockerfile|docker-compose\\.yml|\\.github/workflows/.*\\.yml|infra/|.*\\.tf)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)infrastructure|devops|terraform|docker|ansible|ci/cd"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing infrastructure and DevOps:

      ## Terraform Implementation
      - Implement proper resource management
      - Use proper state management
      - Implement proper module structure
      - Use proper variable handling
      - Follow Terraform best practices

      ## Ansible Configuration
      - Implement proper playbook structure
      - Use proper role organization
      - Implement proper inventory management
      - Use proper variable handling
      - Follow Ansible best practices

      ## Docker Implementation
      - Implement proper containerization
      - Use proper multi-stage builds
      - Implement proper volume management
      - Use proper networking
      - Follow Docker best practices

      ## CI/CD Pipeline
      - Implement proper GitHub Actions
      - Use proper workflow organization
      - Implement proper testing automation
      - Use proper deployment strategies
      - Follow CI/CD best practices

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new Docker container"
    output: "Container uses multi-stage builds, efficient layering, and follows Docker best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>